course: dictionary
lesson: 4460
title: Hard: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer wants. The word hard is a good example. It can mean firm, difficult, using a lot of effort, or strict. Look at the clues in the sentence to decide.
explain: «The hyacinth macaw's beak cracks palm nuts so hard people need a hammer.» Here hard means with great force. The clue is cracks, because breaking a nut takes force. Try the swap: "cracks palm nuts with great force" still makes sense.
explain: «Finding it hard to sit still is not the same as being stupid.» Here hard means difficult, not easy. The clue is finding it, which tells you something is a struggle. Try the swap: "difficult to sit still" makes sense, so hard means difficult.
explain: «They watch him splash past, rolling badly but rowing his hardest.» Here hardest means with the most effort he can give. The clue is rowing, which is work. Hard can change its shape too: hard, harder, hardest.
fact: Hard means firm and not soft, like a rock or a nut.
fact: Hard means difficult, not easy, as in a hard question.
fact: Hard can mean with a lot of effort or force, as in «work hard» or «push hard».
fact: Diamonds are the hardest natural material, so they are very firm.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: A rock is hard, but a sponge is soft. What does hard mean here? | Wet and cold | Easy to play with | *Firm and not soft | Kind and gentle
exercise: Mia says the sum is hard. What does hard mean? | *Difficult, not easy | Firm and not soft | Fast and light | Strict and unkind
exercise: «Ben rowed hard across the lake.» What does hard mean? | Difficult to do | Firm and not soft | *With a lot of effort | Very cold
test: «Finding it hard to sit still is not the same as being stupid.» What does hard mean? | With great force | Kind and gentle | *Difficult, not easy | Firm and not soft
test: «The hyacinth macaw's beak cracks palm nuts so hard people need a hammer.» What does hard mean? | *With great force | Quietly and gently | Strict and unkind | Difficult and not easy
exam: Which sentence uses hard to mean difficult, not easy? | Quiet as a mouse. | She knocked hard on the door. | The bread was hard and stale. | *It was a hard question.
